From c6230e2a0c5c6f9a7631c5a3386cc06e326310e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 08:03:09 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(turning): part-off states the piece kept and a back stock

The Part operation gets one setting, kerf: PartKerf, with two values:
- kept: the cut-off piece (default, the #3452 kerf on the chuck side)
  or the chuck piece (the kerf on the free-end side; a stub comes off).
- back_stock: the whole kerf stands this far off the parting plane,
  into the scrap side (mm, 0 or more).

The kernel and the gouge verdict read the scrap side from kept. The
verdict treats the back stock as part material. A setup that holds the
part end for end now refuses only the default, and the refusal names
the setting. The setting is in the project file (keys written only when
not the default), the Passes tab ("The part is", "Back stock") and MCP
edit_operation, through EditOperationParams. The stamp folds it only
when not the default, so saved ops do not go stale.

Stacked on #3472.

Fixes #3469

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
